# =============================================================================================
# NOTE ON SYNTAX: git does NOT strip trailing inline comments from pattern lines. A line like
#     build/    # some explanation
# is treated as the LITERAL pattern "build/    # some explanation" and matches nothing, so a
# directory meant to be ignored stays committable. Every comment here is therefore on its own
# line. Verify any pattern with:
#     git check-ignore -v <path>
# =============================================================================================

# --- environment + caches --------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store

# --- regenerated pipeline artifacts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt from the pinned source release and the documented library tranches.
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: a bare `data/` matches at ANY depth, which silently excluded the
# src/medchem/data/ SOURCE PACKAGE and left the pushed repo unimportable from a clean clone.
# `/data/*` rather than `/data/`: git does not descend into an EXCLUDED directory, so a negation
# under a plain `/data/` exclusion never matches. The published ChEMBL snapshots are the one thing in
# here that must ship -- hashes prove identity but cannot reconstruct data, so without the bytes the
# frozen metrics are unverifiable. They are 2.7 MB gzipped and CC BY-SA 3.0 (see their README).
/data/*
!/data/frozen_snapshots/
/runs/
/processed/
.medchem_cache/

# --- ChEMBL-derived data ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# ChEMBL is CC BY-SA 3.0. Redistributing curated derivatives carries share-alike + attribution
# obligations, so we ship the SCRIPTS that regenerate them from pinned release 34 instead.
*_training_ic50*.csv
*_curated_ic50*.csv
ALLJAK_*.csv

# --- large or licence-encumbered inputs ------------------------------------------------------
# The ZINC22 library slice (27 MB) and prepared receptor are regenerable from documented queries.
assets/dock_inputs/*.smi
assets/dock_inputs/*.smi.gz
assets/dock_inputs/*.csv.gz
*.prior
*.ckpt
*.joblib
*.pkl

# The scanner's private pattern list. Publishing it would publish the strings it
# exists to detect.
scripts/leak_patterns_local.toml

# --- scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
/tmp/
scratch/
